      ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y^{3}}}-5$ for $y>0$.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y^{3}}}-5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y &= \\int \\left(\\frac{1}{y^{\\frac{3}{2}}}-5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &= \\int y^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y-5\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &= \\frac{y^{-\\frac{3}{2}+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}-5\\frac{y^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{y}}-5y+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
